* The Postfix operator ++ and -- are not working correctly. They are not being parsed with the
correct precedence.
The following example fails to compile correctly
int main(void) {
    int a = 2;
    int d = !(a)--;
    return d;
}

* Improve diagnostics.
  This is quite bad after the parser state, as the location information is lost.
  So, an error from the semantic analyses step will not show the location of the error.
  Making fixing the error quite challenging.
